--   write    only into committed, writable, non-executable data, and only when
--            the whole range lies inside one region; never code, never a
--            protection change (`store` is the same rule by a direct copy)
--   call     only at an address that is committed executable memory, seen when
--            the function is first fetched; the function is kept after that
