  -- each frame costs milliseconds and creates garbage even while this menu is
  -- closed. A new registration wakes discovery immediately; live values below
  -- still follow the host and registry on every step. Older hosts without the
  -- stamp retain discovery, and failed reads are retried rather than cached.
