local ClothingPeers = (function()
-- Peer looks onto local records: assignment instead of negotiation.
--
-- Measured on two machines (research/103, /104): the reserved record a peer
-- wears replicates natively; a record composes once per machine and every
-- actor wearing it renders that composition; and the observer can point a
-- peer's actor at any record by writing that slot's request locally, no
-- ownership involved. So a peer's look is composed on a record this client
-- chooses for that peer out of the slot's reserved records, which are one
-- shared pool whatever pack a look belongs to (research/105): the record the
-- peer's actor already wears here when it is free, else the lowest free one,
-- and the same look shares a record. The record the local actor wears is
-- never anybody else's. Nobody moves. A pool that runs out renders whatever
-- the peer's own record holds, logged once. The remote module applies the
-- assignment to the actors; nothing here touches one. Records the remote
-- module reports as occupied (an actor renders them or streams toward them)
