-- own authorisation is re-evaluated continuously after startup, through the
-- injected `plan`: the saved record still defines the carrier and the actor
-- wears the login fallback instead. A settled, stable loss opens one episode:
-- headless equips with retries, reported when the carrier is back on or the
-- episode is abandoned, and never repeated until the carrier has been seen
