--                check changes state or a check is added.
--   console      one line, for when no file can be written:
--                `[HD2Transmog] health=pass`, or the overall state and every
--                check that is degraded, off or partial. It is printed at
--                the first reading at which no `game.*` check is still
--                unknown, or twenty seconds after the start, whichever comes
--                first: a line spent before the game was looked at would say
--                nothing about it. One more line, and no more in a session,
--                the first time a check is degraded or off that was not in
--                the line already printed.
--   STATUS.txt   the checks that are degraded or off, after the stages that
--                did not start.
--   alive.txt    `alive <seconds>` at the first second and then every five,
--                for the first two minutes only: if the game closes itself
--                the last value is when.
--   problems.txt the log's ledger (`Diagnostics` `problems()`): what the
--                player was shown and the problems. One second after the
--                start, `none` included; at the next reading after a new
--                entry; after a repeat's count alone, at most every RETRY.
--
-- The checks are read once a second and no more; between those the schedule
-- compares one number a frame and does not enter this stage. A file that
-- cannot be written is said once until it is written again, and left alone
-- for half a minute. Nothing here raises, and nothing else depends on this
-- stage.
